      "p0001-ocr-l0028"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Second, an evaluation of the dual-stage XGBoost model's prediction performance was carried out. The model demonstrated outstanding performance in predicting the 2021 and 2024 Olympic Games, achieving a classification accuracy of 95% and an overall prediction accuracy of 68%, significantly outperforming existing Olympic prediction models. Confidence interval estimation was conducted using the non-parametric Bootstrap method. After 1000 iterative ver- ifications, the model's sample coverage probability exceeded 0.95, and the probability that the predicted values fell within the confidence interval was over 70%. Based on these results, we predicted the medal distribution for the 2028 Olympic Games. Moreover, we innovatively combined the classifier and regressor to quantify the first-time medal-winning probability of small Olympic countries. Simultaneously, SHAP value analysis was utilized to uncover the"
  },
